    "content": "As of early 2025, Pam Bondi is a staunch ally of Donald Trump, selected by him to serve as the United States Attorney General. A former Florida Attorney General, she previously served on his first impeachment defense team and led the legal team at the pro-Trump America First Policy Institute. Here are the key aspects of her relationship with Trump: Role in Administration: Trump appointed her as U.S. Attorney General, citing her work on his Opioid and Drug Abuse Commission during his first term. Longtime Ally: She has been a loyal supporter since 2016, endorsing him early in the primary over her home-state Senator, Marco Rubio. Legal Defense: She was part of Trump's defense team during his first Senate impeachment trial and appeared at his 2024 hush money trial in a show of support. Policy Positions: As a member of the America First Policy Institute, she helped build the policy groundwork for his second term. She has supported his claims regarding the 2020 election and criticized investigations into him, says the League of Conservation Voters, Senate Committee on the Judiciary and Common Cause. Her selection as Attorney General was announced in November 2024 following the withdrawal of Matt Gaetz, noted by The Guardian and Associated Press News.",
